{
  "$comment": "Golden cases of the port from page_config sections to builder nodes. `legacy` is a PageSection as Django stores it (snake_case props, the section title); `node` is the node it becomes: settings camelCased, `title` a setting, every array of objects a list of child blocks. Ids are compared by position (the first child is b1), never by value. The storefront parses `node` and must hand the section component exactly the props the legacy section gave it (test/unit/server/utils/builderPortFixtures.spec.ts); Django's data migration must produce `node` from `legacy` (the same file is its test input).",
